Subject: ps2xRuntime: observers for the GIF stream per path and for register writes outside it

GifArbiter::setObserver sees every packet just before the GS processes it, in processing order, with its
path. The data is the path's GIF stream: a packet can start with bytes the runtime added (streamOffset), the
GIFtag the VIF1 interpreter puts in front of an IMAGE transfer that continues in a later DIRECT; the observer
does not see those. GS::setRegisterObserver sees GS::writeRegister calls, the register writes runtime handlers
make outside the GIF stream (sceGsPutDrawEnv). Rule of Rose uses both to write PCSX2 GS dumps.

